{"agent":"fix-mcp-setup","data":{"item":"","summary":"review.split_diff emits a HEADER-ONLY chunk (diff --git ... +++ b/<file>, no @@ hunk) when a file's first hunk would overflow max_chunk_chars: the header plus the lone newline before '@@' is flushed as its own piece. The reviewer then reports the file as empty. Reproduced: a new 151-line test file at max_chunk_chars=5000 splits into a 175-char header-only chunk + the 6430-char hunk; rubber_duck on B-fix-mcp-setup-init flagged tests/test_setup_writes_init.py as 'zero bytes'. Fix: do not count the pre-hunk remainder as content (compare current.strip() to header.strip()) before flushing."},"id":"e6f04eaba076c59d8c50d6be0","kind":"bug.found","lamport":5091,"schema":1,"subject":"Bc1f52d9244","ts":"2026-09-30T20:05:32.697334Z"}
